# HostSeal APT repository, deb822 format.
#
# This file is installed at /etc/apt/sources.list.d/hostseal.sources. It is host-facing, so it explains
# only what a person reading it on their own machine needs: why the key is named here rather than added
# to the system keyring. The choice of URL is a maintainer decision and is documented in
# packaging/README.md, where the person making it will be — a host is not where that argument belongs,
# and the placeholder below is substituted on the URIs line only, so this comment stays true after it.
#
# Signed-By names an explicit keyring, so the HostSeal signing key is trusted for the HostSeal repository
# and for nothing else. apt-key is never used: it installs a key trusted for every repository on the
# system, which turns one compromised project into root on the machine.

Types: deb
URIs: @@APT_URL@@
Suites: stable
Components: main
Architectures: amd64 arm64
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/hostseal-archive-keyring.gpg
